.TH AD_LAYER_SKIP_INDENT 1 "2026-08-30" "ad 2.0" "ad layers"
.SH NAME
ad_layer_skip_indent \- skip animation for indent-only hunks (apply ops instantly)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_layer_skip_indent
.RI [ options ]
< post_ops > marked_ops
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ad_layer_skip_indent
detects hunks where ALL changes are whitespace (spaces, tabs, or newlines).
These are "indent-only" hunks — the content is unchanged, only the leading
whitespace changed.
.PP
When an indent-only hunk is detected, the layer wraps its ops with special
delay markers. The pace layer recognizes these markers and sets all delays
to 0 (instant) within the marked region, then adds a pause after.
.PP
The ops are NOT modified — they're all still applied, so the buffer ends up
correct. Only the animation timing is affected: the viewer sees the indent
change applied instantly (no character-by-character animation) followed by
a brief pause.
.SH HOW IT WORKS
.PP
.RS
.nf
Input hunk (indent-only):
  delete space, delete space, insert space x8, keep 'f'

Output (with markers):
  delay  -1  0  0        ← indent_skip_start (line=-1, col=0)
  delete space           ← original ops, unchanged
  delete space
  insert space x8
  keep 'f'
  delay  -1  1  300      ← indent_skip_end (line=-1, col=1, pause=300ms)
.fi
.RE
.PP
The pace layer sees the start marker, enters "skip mode" (all delays = 0),
applies the ops instantly, then sees the end marker and emits a 300ms pause.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-pause\-after\-ms  N
Pause duration (ms) after an indent-only hunk. Default: 300.
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Show help and exit.
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
V2 TSV format. Input should be post-reorder (see
.BR ad_layer_reorder (1)).
Runs BEFORE pace (it's a postprocess layer, not a pipeline stage).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ad_layer_skip_indent < reordered_ops.txt > marked_ops.txt
Mark indent-only hunks for instant application.
.TP
.B ad_layer_skip_indent --pause-after-ms 500 < reordered_ops.txt > marked_ops.txt
Use 500ms pause after indent-only hunks.
.SH USAGE IN PIPELINE
.PP
Add this layer between reorder and pace:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ad_postprocess \\
  --ad-layer=ad_layer_reorder \\
  --ad-layer=ad_layer_skip_indent \\
  < raw_ops.txt | ad_layer_pace > timed_ops.txt
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ad_postprocess (1),
.BR ad_layer_reorder (1),
.BR ad_layer_pace (1)
.PP
.I docs/src/plugin-layers.md
